  "headline": "Monster Hunter Wilds Beginner's Guide: Everything New Players Need to Know",
  "description": "A beginner-friendly primer for Monster Hunter Wilds covering core gameplay systems, recommended weapons, and early game tips for new players.",
  "articleBody": "Monster Hunter Wilds is the latest entry in Capcom's action RPG franchise, released in February 2025 for PS5, Xbox Series X|S, and PC. This guide covers the essentials for players new to the Monster Hunter series.\n\n■ Overview\nPlayers take on the role of a Hunter, exploring vast open-world environments to track and defeat large monsters. The core gameplay loop involves hunting monsters, collecting materials, and crafting stronger weapons and armor to take on tougher challenges. Online co-op for up to four players is supported.\n\n■ Beginner-Friendly Weapons (out of 14 total)\nGreat Sword: High single-hit damage with simple controls. Can also block attacks.\nLong Sword: Long reach with satisfying counter mechanics via the Foresight Slash. One of the most popular weapons.\nSword & Shield: A versatile all-rounder that allows item use while unsheathed. Can block and has high survivability.\nLight Bowgun: A ranged weapon for safely attacking from a distance. Requires ammo management but makes it easy to observe monster patterns.\n\n■ Early Game Progression\n1. Complete the tutorial: Learn the basic controls and hunting flow.\n2. Visit the Training Area: Test all 14 weapons to find your preferred playstyle.\n3. Gather materials on gathering quests: Stock up on potions, traps, and crafting materials before combat.\n4. Clear Low Rank quests in order: The story unlocks new monsters and areas as you progress.\n\n■ New Features in Wilds\nSeamless Open World: Explore environments without loading screens between zones.\nDynamic Environment System: Weather and time of day affect monster behavior patterns.\nSeikret Companion: A rideable companion for traversal and combat support.\nFocus Mode: A new aiming system that makes targeting monster weak points more intuitive.\n\n■ Tips for New Hunters\nThere is no experience point loss on death. A quest fails after three carts, but you can retry unlimited times. Firing an SOS Flare in multiplayer lets other hunters join your quest. Observe monster movements carefully and punish openings after attacks. Early on, prioritize armor with high defense over specific skills.\n\nThis article is an introductory overview for series newcomers. Detailed weapon guides and advanced strategies will be covered in separate articles.",
